*Revision:* A previous version of this press release included incorrect foo=
d distribution times. The food distribution times have been updated to refl=
ect the correct schedule.

---

Sept. 21, 4 p.m., County of Kaua=CA=BBi, Hurricane Lowell Recovery

L=C4=AAHU=CA=BBE =E2=80=93 Hurricane Lowell recovery continues across Kaua=
=CA=BBi. Here are the latest updates.

=C2=A0

*Phone lines restored*

General phone lines for the following County departments are now back in se=
rvice:


  * The Agency on Elderly Affairs: (808) 241-4470=20
  * The Department of Human Resources: (808) 241-4956=20
  * The Office of the Prosecuting Attorney: (808) 241-1888=20

=C2=A0

*Weather outlook*

Officials are monitoring a developing weather system that is the remnants o=
f former Tropical Depression Fifteen-E. The system could bring increased wi=
nds beginning Wednesday night, with potential for stronger winds at higher =
elevations going into the weekend. The system=E2=80=99s track and strength =
remain uncertain, and potential impacts for Kaua=CA=BBi have not been deter=
mined. Residents should continue to monitor official weather updates as the=
 system develops.

=C2=A0

*Kaua=E2=80=98i Sunshine Markets*

Several farmers markets are reopening this week:


  * Monday: Kukui Grove Pau Hana Market, 3 - 5:30 p.m., L=C4=ABhu=CA=BBe.=20
  * Tuesday: Coconut Marketplace, 9 a.m. - 1 p.m., Kapa=CA=BBa.=20
  * Wednesday: Kapa=CA=BBa Sunshine Market, 3 - 4:30 p.m., Kapa=CA=BBa; Kau=
a=CA=BBi Culinary Market, 3:30 - 6 p.m., Po=CA=BBip=C5=AB.=20
  * Thursday: Coconut Marketplace, 9 a.m. - 1 p.m., Kapa=CA=BBa; Hale Puna,=
 3 - 5 p.m., Waimea.=20
  * Saturday: Grove Farm Market, starting at 9:30 a.m. until supplies last,=
 L=C4=ABhu=CA=BBe.=20

For more information about Sunshine Markets, call the Office of Economic De=
velopment at (808) 241-4946.

=C2=A0

*Neighborhood Centers *

Now open:


  * Kekaha Neighborhood Center (patio only for previously scheduled parties=
)=20
  * Waimea Neighborhood Center (side rooms only; main hall closed due to da=
mage)=20
  * Waimea Smokey Valley Clubhouse=20
  * Hanap=C4=93p=C4=93 Neighborhood Center and Multipurpose Center=20
  * Kalaheo Neighborhood Center=20
  * L=C4=ABhu=CA=BBe Neighborhood Center (old and new)=20
  * Anahola Clubhouse=20

=C2=A0

*North Shore refuse collection resumes*

Solid Waste crews will collect refuse in H=C4=81=CA=BBena and Wainiha on Tu=
esday, Sept. 22. Powerhouse Road remains inaccessible, but crews will servi=
ce carts brought down to K=C5=ABhi=C5=8D Highway. Regular North Shore refus=
e collection will take place Thursday, Sept. 24.

=C2=A0

*Hurricane resource centers*

Starting Monday, the Hanalei and K=C5=8Dloa hurricane resource centers will=
 be open daily from 9 a.m. to 4 p.m.

Unemployment insurance: State staff from the Department of Labor and Indust=
rial Relations (DLIR) will provide in-person support with unemployment insu=
rance applications. DLIR staff will be in Hanalei Sept. 21-22 and K=C5=8Dlo=
a Sept. 23-24. The County encourages residents who have experienced challen=
ges applying online to meet with DLIR staff in person.

SNAP benefits: DHS staff will be on site at both the K=C5=8Dloa and Hanalei=
 hurricane resource centers on Tuesday, Sept. 22, and Thursday, Sept. 24, t=
o provide in-person support with SNAP benefits.

The Hanalei Initiative runs an hourly shuttle, starting at 9 a.m., from The=
 Hanalei Colony Resort to the Hanalei Hurricane Resource Center.

=C2=A0

*Emergency food distributions this week*


  *=20

Tuesday, Sept. 22: Waip=C4=81 Foundation, Hanalei, noon to 2 p.m. (walk-up;=
 bring reusable bags); =CA=BB=C4=80ina Ho=CA=BBokupu o K=C4=ABlauea, 4045 K=
=C4=ABlauea Road, 3 to 5 p.m.


  *=20

Wednesday, Sept. 23: St. Raphael Church, K=C5=8Dloa, 4 to 6 p.m.


  *=20

Thursday, Sept. 24: Westside Christian Center, Kekaha, 10 a.m. to noon; Lim=
a Ola, =CA=BBEle=CA=BBele, 2:15 to 4:15 p.m.; Aloha Church, L=C4=ABhu=CA=BB=
e, 4 to 6 p.m.


  *=20

Friday, Sept. 25: Hale L=C4=ABhu=CA=BBe, 4286 Rice St., 3 to 5 p.m.

=C2=A0

*L=C4=ABhu=CA=BBe Civic Center and property tax deadline*

In-person services at the L=C4=ABhu=CA=BBe Civic Center remain closed while=
 computer systems are restored after the Sept. 9 K=C4=81pule Building fire.=
 County offices outside the Civic Center remain open. The Real Property Div=
ision is the exception on campus, offering in-person help at the Purchasing=
 Office, 8 a.m. to 4 p.m. weekdays, ahead of the Sept. 30 exemption filing =
deadline.

Property owners who applied but did not receive an emailed confirmation sho=
uld resubmit, as paperwork was destroyed in the fire. Submit by email to rp=
assessment@kauai.gov (preferred), by mail, or at one of two drop boxes: the=
 Mo=CA=BBikeha Building, ground floor, Monday through Friday from 7:45 a.m.=
 to 4:30 p.m., and the Pi=CA=BBikoi Building fronting Rice Street. Storm-da=
maged property owners have until June 30, 2027, to file for disaster tax re=
lief at kauai.gov/lowellrealproperty [ https://www.kauai.gov/Residents/Repo=
rt-Hurricane-Lowell-Property-Damage?utm_medium=3Demail&utm_source=3Dgovdeli=
very ].

DMV counter services remain unavailable. Vehicle registration renewal optio=
ns are posted at www.kauairecovers.org [ http://www.kauairecovers.org/?utm_=
medium=3Demail&utm_source=3Dgovdelivery ].

=C2=A0

*Power*

KIUC reported 98% of members restored as of Monday afternoon. Crews continu=
e work on the North Shore between Moloa=CA=BBa and Hanalei and on scattered=
 outages between Kapa=CA=BBa and Kekaha. Clearing continues in Wainiha, H=
=C4=81=CA=BBena and K=C5=8Dke=CA=BBe so crews can safely reach damaged equi=
pment.

Do not approach utility crews or enter work areas. Members needing a paymen=
t plan or financial help can visit kiuc.coop/payment-assistance [ https://k=
iuc.coop/payment-assistance?utm_medium=3Demail&utm_source=3Dgovdelivery ]. =
For questions, call (808) 246-4300. Outage map: kiuc.outagemap.coop [ https=
://kiuc.outagemap.coop/?utm_medium=3Demail&utm_source=3Dgovdelivery#/ ]

=C2=A0

*Roads*

State crews continue debris removal along Kaumuali=CA=BBi and K=C5=ABhi=C5=
=8D highways. K=C5=ABhi=C5=8D Highway from Princeville to K=C4=93=CA=BB=C4=
=93 is open to local traffic only. The weight restriction on Wainiha River =
Bridge No. 3 has been lifted to 15 tons. Travel only if necessary, since ex=
tra traffic slows debris removal, power restoration and road repairs.

=C2=A0

*Some state lands reopen *

DLNR reopened parts of Wailua River State Park, the Waimea Valley section o=
f Pu=CA=BBu Ka Pele Forest Reserve, and Hunting Unit F this morning at 6:30=
 a.m., with restrictions. Uluwehi Falls, N=C4=81 Ala Hele trails and K=C5=
=8Dke=CA=BBe Road remain closed, and most DLNR lands stay closed. Details a=
t dlnr.hawaii.gov [ https://dlnr.hawaii.gov/?utm_medium=3Demail&utm_source=
=3Dgovdelivery ].

=C2=A0

*Other updates*


  * The Sept. 8 Planning Commission meeting has been rescheduled to Oct. 13=
. Agenda items originally scheduled for the Oct. 13 meeting will also be co=
nsidered at this meeting.=C2=A0For more information, please contact the Pla=
nning Department at 808-241-4050 or visit kauai.gov/Planning-Commission [ h=
ttp://www.kauai.gov/Planning-Commission?utm_medium=3Demail&utm_source=3Dgov=
delivery ].=20
  * The K=C4=ABlauea Refuge Area remains open at K=C4=ABlauea Neighborhood =
Center, 2460 Keneke St. This refuge area will close on Tuesday, Sept. 22, a=
t 10 a.m. All remaining refuge area residents have been offered the opportu=
nity to connect with housing case management and other wraparound services =
and support.=20
  * Households that lost food to power outages may be eligible for replacem=
ent SNAP benefits. Details at hawaii.gov [ https://humanservices.hawaii.gov=
/?utm_medium=3Demail&utm_source=3Dgovdelivery ].=20
  * The island wide Brown Water Advisory for Kaua=E2=80=98i has been cancel=
led; however, a Brown Water Advisory has been issued for various areas arou=
nd the island. Stay out of floodwater and ocean water near stream mouths an=
d drains. For more information visit the Hawai=CA=BBi Department of Health =
Clean Water Branch System at eha-cloud.doh.hawaii.gov/cwb. [ https://eha-cl=
oud.doh.hawaii.gov/cwb/?utm_medium=3Demail&utm_source=3Dgovdelivery#!/landi=
ng ]=20
  * Water Conservation Notices remain for the =CA=BBAnini, H=C4=81=CA=BBena=
-Wainiha and K=C4=ABlauea systems. Report outages or leaks at (808) 245-544=
4.=20
  * Seven debris and refuse sites are open islandwide, with tipping fees wa=
ived for storm debris. Hours and accepted materials are at kauairecovers.or=
g/debris [ http://www.kauairecovers.org/debris?utm_medium=3Demail&utm_sourc=
e=3Dgovdelivery ].=20
  * Kaua=CA=BBi Bus fares are waived through Sept. 30; the 900 and 950 expr=
ess routes are not running.=20
  * Several County beach parks, both the Waimea and Kapa=CA=BBa pools, and =
Wailua Golf Course remain closed.=20

=C2=A0

*Report storm damage*

Residents are still encouraged to report storm damage, which helps show the=
 extent of the damage across the island and may help Kaua=CA=BBi qualify fo=
r state and federal aid. File at bit.ly/kauaidamage [ https://survey123.arc=
gis.com/share/54d0b90fb9a74a1094e89d9f26b5d759?utm_medium=3Demail&utm_sourc=
e=3Dgovdelivery ], report roadway and public space hazards at bit.ly/kauaih=
azard [ https://survey123.arcgis.com/share/060659e0fd7344d59ccb2056dcbe53f9=
?utm_medium=3Demail&utm_source=3Dgovdelivery ], and businesses can report a=
t bit.ly/lowelldamage [ https://survey123.arcgis.com/share/f828eb79bd884e6b=
bc54535007ba9bf9?utm_medium=3Demail&utm_source=3Dgovdelivery ]. Still file =
a claim with your insurance company.

=C2=A0

*Contact County offices*

Use interim numbers until phone lines are restored: General (808) 726-0702;=
 Secondary (808) 347-9833; DMV (808) 241-1949. Voicemails may not be retrie=
vable.

To sign up for Everbridge, the County's emergency notification service, vis=
it www.kauai.gov/KEMA [ http://www.kauai.gov/KEMA?utm_medium=3Demail&utm_so=
urce=3Dgovdelivery ] and click "Notification Services," text "KAUAIEMA" to =
888777, or call KEMA at (808) 241-1800.

For recovery help and updates, visit www.kauairecovers.org [ http://www.kau=
airecovers.org/?utm_medium=3Demail&utm_source=3Dgovdelivery ] or call 211.

